<div class="container">

<header class="main-header">
  <div class="book-title">Likutay Halachos &middot; Orach Chaim</div>
  <h1>Hilchos Tisha B&rsquo;Av v&rsquo;Ta&rsquo;aniyos</h1>
  <div class="subtitle">Halacha 3</div>
  <div class="halacha-num">The matter of the four fasts that we fast over the<br>Churban [destruction of the] Bais HaMikdash</div>
  <div class="source-ref-header">Based on the ma&rsquo;amar &ldquo;B&rsquo;Raishis l&rsquo;aynay kol Yisrael&rdquo;<br>[&ldquo;In the beginning&rdquo; &mdash; &ldquo;before the eyes of all Yisrael&rdquo;]<br>in Likutay Tinyana, siman 67</div>
</header>

<p class="no-indent">And the general rule is that the <span class="concept">Tzaddik of truth</span> [<span class="heb-term">Tzaddik ha&rsquo;emes</span>] is the grace [<span class="heb-term">chain</span>], the beauty [<span class="heb-term">p&rsquo;air</span>], and the splendor [<span class="heb-term">y&rsquo;fi</span>] of all the worlds, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;and Yosef was beautiful of form and beautiful of appearance&rdquo;</span> <span class="verse-source">(B&rsquo;raishis 39:6)</span>, etc. And through him one can gaze at oneself, in all the dimensions [<span class="heb-term">midos</span>] that come from the four foundations [<span class="heb-term">arba y&rsquo;sodos</span>] &mdash; how he holds fast to them. For all the four foundations are drawn from the Tzaddik, who is the aspect of <span class="concept">y&rsquo;sod haP&rsquo;shut</span> [the foundation of the simple meaning], the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Tzaddik y&rsquo;sod olam&rdquo;</span> [the righteous one is the foundation of the world], etc., the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;and a river goes out from Eden to water&rdquo;</span> <span class="verse-source">(B&rsquo;raishis 2:10)</span>, etc. And they were the four heads [of the rivers], etc. For His Name [<span class="heb-term">Sh&rsquo;mo</span>] is enmeshed [<span class="heb-term">mishtateif</span>] in eight, etc. And the Name of Hashem is in the aspect of four letters [<span class="heb-term">oaseyos</span>]. And from there the four foundations chain down, and at the outset they are in the aspect of <span class="concept">four appearances</span> [<span class="heb-term">arba mar&rsquo;os</span>] &mdash; the aspect of three colors of the eye [<span class="heb-term">g&rsquo;vanim d&rsquo;ayna</span>] and the pupil [<span class="heb-term">bas ayin</span>], etc. And this is the aspect of <span class="concept">Shabbas</span>, etc. And therefore Shabbas, which is the aspect of three colors of the eye and <span class="heb-term">bas ayin</span>, shines [<span class="heb-term">m&rsquo;ir</span>] to the Bais HaMikdash, etc. And all of this is the aspect of the <span class="concept">lights of light</span> [<span class="heb-term">m&rsquo;oray ha&rsquo;or</span>]. And when the Bais HaMikdash was destroyed, this is the aspect of the <span class="concept">departure of the lights of light</span> [<span class="heb-term">histalkus m&rsquo;oray or</span>], and then the <span class="heb-term">chas v&rsquo;shalom</span> [G-d forbid] gained strength &mdash; the <span class="concept">lights of fire</span> [<span class="heb-term">m&rsquo;oray aish</span>], in the aspect of &ldquo;from the bitter He sent fire,&rdquo; etc. And this is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;and fire went out in Tzion and consumed its foundations&rdquo;</span> <span class="verse-source">(Aichah 4:11)</span>, etc. For through the churban of the Bais HaMikdash &mdash; the aspect of the departure of the lights of light &mdash; the lights of fire gained strength, and through this all the four foundations [<span class="heb-term">y&rsquo;sodos</span>] are damaged. For the <span class="heb-term">tikkun</span> [rectification] of all the four foundations, which are the totality of all the <span class="heb-term">midos</span> [dimensions], is through the lights of light drawn from the Tzaddik, from the aspect of Shabbas, which was shining in the Bais HaMikdash, etc. (See there, all this is well explained.)</p>

<!-- OAS ALEF -->
<div class="section-marker">1</div>

<p class="no-indent">And therefore the <span class="concept">bond</span> [<span class="heb-term">k&rsquo;shura / hiskashrus</span>] to <span class="concept">Tzaddikim</span> is even more [important] than the Churban [destruction] of the Bais HaMikdash. For the main purpose of the lights of light [<span class="heb-term">m&rsquo;oray or</span>] is drawn from the Tzaddik, who is the aspect of Shabbas that shines to the Bais HaMikdash. And therefore anyone who has in him <span class="heb-term">Daas</span> [awareness/knowledge] as if the Bais HaMikdash were built in his days &mdash; for when there is in him <span class="heb-term">Daas</span>, which is the <span class="heb-term">m&rsquo;chin</span> [the brains/consciousness] &mdash; this is the aspect of the Tzaddik whose generation merits to know and to have <span class="heb-term">m&rsquo;chin</span>, which are the aspect of lights of light, etc. It is certainly as if the Bais HaMikdash were built in his days, for the main purpose of the building and the existence of the Bais HaMikdash is through the <span class="heb-term">Daas</span> and the <span class="heb-term">m&rsquo;chin</span>, which are the aspect of the lights of light that shine to the Bais HaMikdash, as above.</p>

<!-- OAS BAIS -->
<div class="section-marker">2</div>

<p class="no-indent">And this is the aspect of the <span class="concept">four fasts</span> [<span class="heb-term">arba ta&rsquo;aniyos</span>] that we need to fast over the Churban of the Bais HaMikdash, which is the aspect of the departure of the lights of light [<span class="heb-term">histalkus m&rsquo;oray or</span>], etc., <span class="heb-term">chas v&rsquo;shalom</span>, as above. For the main purpose of eating in holiness [<span class="heb-term">achilah bi&rsquo;k&rsquo;dusha</span>] is through the lights of light drawn from the Tzaddik of truth, through whom all the four foundations [<span class="heb-term">y&rsquo;sodos</span>] are rectified and clarified, as above. For all types of food are included in the four foundations, as is known. And therefore they are also the vitality [<span class="heb-term">chiyus</span>] of the body, for every [body part] is also from the four foundations. And therefore when the lights of light are illuminated through the Tzaddik &mdash; which is the aspect of building the Bais HaMikdash &mdash; through this, all the four foundations are rectified, as above. Then [there is] eating in holiness, in the aspect of the Tzaddik &ldquo;eats to satisfy his soul&rdquo; [<span class="heb-term">ochail l&rsquo;sova nafsho</span>] <span class="verse-source">(Mishlai 13:25)</span>. And then all the four foundations are included in holiness, firmly rooted within the foundation of the simple meaning [<span class="heb-term">y&rsquo;sod haP&rsquo;shut</span>]. And then all the four foundations are included in the aspect of the lights of light, which is the aspect of <span class="heb-term">m&rsquo;chin</span> [consciousness], the aspect of the light of the Tzaddik, as above. And then eating in holiness, including the <span class="heb-term">n&rsquo;shamah</span> [soul], which is also the aspect of <span class="heb-term">m&rsquo;chin</span>, the aspect of lights of light, the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;and the soul of his masters are within them&rdquo;</span>. And the body [<span class="heb-term">guf</span>] is the aspect of lights of fire [<span class="heb-term">m&rsquo;oray aish</span>], for fire [<span class="heb-term">aish</span>] is the foremost [<span class="heb-term">harishon</span>] of the four foundations. And all the desires [<span class="heb-term">ta&rsquo;avos</span>] of the body all come from fire, and the heat of the body that gives rise to all the desires. It emerges that the main <span class="heb-term">tikkun</span> of eating in holiness is through the <span class="concept">Tzaddik of truth</span>, through whom all the four foundations are rectified and included firmly in the aspect of lights of light, the aspect of <span class="heb-term">m&rsquo;chin</span>, and then eating in holiness, including the <span class="heb-term">n&rsquo;shamah</span>, which is also the aspect of <span class="heb-term">m&rsquo;chin</span>, the aspect of lights of light. And this is the aspect of &ldquo;the Tzaddik &lsquo;eats to satisfy his soul&rsquo;&rdquo; [<span class="heb-term">Tzaddik ochail l&rsquo;sova nafsho</span>], as above. And therefore all the <span class="concept">sustenance and plenty</span> [<span class="heb-term">hashpa&rsquo;os</span> and <span class="heb-term">s&rsquo;vi&rsquo;ah</span>] are drawn from the Tzaddik of the generation, in the aspect of Yosef &mdash; who is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;and a river goes out from Eden to water&rdquo;</span>, etc. For all things are drawn from the four foundations, which are all drawn from the Tzaddik, etc., as above &mdash; who is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;and a river goes out from Eden to water&rdquo;</span> the garden [<span class="heb-term">gan</span>], as above. For the Tzaddik waters and irrigates the land [<span class="heb-term">ha&rsquo;aretz</span>], for through him are drawn all the <span class="heb-term">hashpa&rsquo;os</span> [sustenance]. For all the rains and the produce [<span class="heb-term">matar</span>] descend through the Tzaddik, as is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Hashem does not rain upon the land, and there is no person&rdquo;</span> <span class="verse-source">(B&rsquo;raishis 2:5)</span>, etc. &mdash; meaning that the Tzaddik, through whom all the rains are drawn to the entire face of the earth, for he is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;and a river goes out from Eden to water&rdquo;</span>, etc., and from there it separates, etc. And therefore all the <span class="heb-term">hashpa&rsquo;os</span> are drawn through the Tzaddik, in the aspect of &ldquo;Yosef sustains [<span class="heb-term">y&rsquo;chalkel</span>] his father and his brothers,&rdquo; the aspect of &ldquo;and all the land came to Mitzrayim to Yosef to procure [grain],&rdquo; for Yosef is the ruler [<span class="heb-term">ha&rsquo;shalit</span>] &mdash; he is the provider [<span class="heb-term">ha&rsquo;mashbir</span>], etc. For Yosef, who is the ruler &mdash; who is the Tzaddik of the generation, from whom are drawn all the four foundations &mdash; he is the head of the household [<span class="heb-term">rosh habayis</span>], etc. (as explained in the ma&rsquo;amar as above) &mdash; who is [the aspect of] <span class="verse">&ldquo;a river goes out from Eden to water&rdquo;</span>, etc. &mdash; he is the provider. For from him are drawn all the plenty [<span class="heb-term">s&rsquo;vi&rsquo;os</span>] and all the sustenance [<span class="heb-term">hashpa&rsquo;os</span>], which are all included in the four foundations that are drawn from the Tzaddik, as above.</p>

<!-- OAS GIMMEL -->
<div class="section-marker">3</div>

<p class="no-indent">And therefore there is a great <span class="concept">mitzvah to eat on Shabbas</span>, as is written: &ldquo;eat it today, for today is Shabbas for Hashem&rdquo; <span class="verse-source">(Sh&rsquo;mos 16:25)</span>. For on Shabbas they illuminate [<span class="heb-term">m&rsquo;irin</span>] the aspect of lights of light [<span class="heb-term">m&rsquo;oray or</span>], as above. And then eating in holiness [<span class="heb-term">achilah bi&rsquo;k&rsquo;dusha</span>] is accomplished, as above. And therefore there is a mitzvah to eat on Shabbas. And this is what the Torah was given with the taste [<span class="heb-term">ta&rsquo;am</span>] of eating Shabbas &mdash; because Shabbas is the aspect of lights of light. And this is what is written: &ldquo;eat it today&rdquo; &mdash; for &ldquo;Shabbas today for Hashem.&rdquo; &ldquo;See&rdquo; [<span class="heb-term">R&rsquo;u</span>] &mdash; specifically, for this is the aspect of lights of light, which are the aspect of &ldquo;seeing&rdquo; [<span class="heb-term">r&rsquo;iyah</span>], the aspect of three colors of the eye and <span class="heb-term">bas ayin</span> [pupil] (as explained in the ma&rsquo;amar as above, on this passage; see there). And therefore, because Shabbas is the aspect of &ldquo;seeing&rdquo; [<span class="heb-term">r&rsquo;iyah</span>] &mdash; the aspect of lights of light &mdash; therefore &ldquo;eat it today,&rdquo; for because of this there is a mitzvah to eat on Shabbas, for then eating in holiness when they illuminate the lights of light, the aspect of the Tzaddik of truth, the aspect of the Bais HaMikdash, as above.</p>

<!-- OAS DALED -->
<div class="section-marker">4</div>

<p class="no-indent">And therefore, when the Bais HaMikdash was destroyed and the lights of light [<span class="heb-term">m&rsquo;oray or</span>] departed, it was decreed to fast four fasts [<span class="heb-term">arba tzomos</span>]. For now, when the lights of light departed through the Churban of the Bais HaMikdash, it became hard to eat in holiness, as above. For then the <span class="concept">four foundations are damaged in their physicality</span> [<span class="heb-term">gashmiyus</span>], which are the aspect of lights of fire [<span class="heb-term">m&rsquo;oray aish</span>], etc., as above. Since the lights of light departed, the four foundations are damaged, and on the contrary, rather, the eating was hard to eat in holiness, and therefore they need to fast four fasts and then to subdue the four foundations through this &mdash; and to merit through the fasts to return and to illuminate the aspect of lights of light which are the <span class="heb-term">m&rsquo;chin</span> [consciousness/brains], as above. For when the lights of light departed, which is the aspect of Shabbas that illuminates to the Bais HaMikdash &mdash; when the Bais HaMikdash was destroyed, the light of Shabbas was concealed &mdash; and then there is no eating in holiness. When there is no eating in holiness, the four foundations are included in their physicality [<span class="heb-term">gashmiyus</span>], the aspect of lights of fire. And all the desires [<span class="heb-term">ta&rsquo;avos</span>] of the body come through fire and the heat of the body, from [the aspect of] <span class="heb-term">machlokes</span> [strife/division] (as explained in the words of Rabbainu, of blessed memory). It emerges that through the sins [<span class="heb-term">avonos</span>] that damaged the <span class="heb-term">machlokes</span> [strife] and gave power, <span class="heb-term">chas v&rsquo;shalom</span>, to the <span class="heb-term">Sitra Achara</span> [Other Side] &mdash; which prevails over holiness [<span class="heb-term">k&rsquo;dusha</span>] &mdash; therefore <span class="heb-term">dinim</span> [harsh judgments], <span class="heb-term">chas v&rsquo;shalom</span>, are aroused upon him, and those <span class="heb-term">dinim</span> place upon him the distresses [<span class="heb-term">tzaros</span>], <span class="heb-term">chas v&rsquo;shalom</span>, which are as if in opposition to [his] will &mdash; the aspect of <span class="heb-term">machlokes</span>. And therefore the <span class="heb-term">tikkun</span> for all this is <span class="heb-term">ta&rsquo;anis</span> [fasting]. For the general rule is that in opposition to every type of <span class="heb-term">machlokes</span>, the <span class="heb-term">tikkun</span> is <span class="heb-term">ta&rsquo;anis</span>, in the aspect of &ldquo;abundant peace&rdquo; [<span class="heb-term">marbeh tz&rsquo;dakah, marbeh shalom</span>]. And the main purpose of <span class="heb-term">ta&rsquo;anis</span> is <span class="heb-term">tz&rsquo;dakah</span> [charity/righteousness], for &ldquo;the reward of a fast is the charity&rdquo; [<span class="heb-term">agra d&rsquo;sa&rsquo;anisa tzidkasa</span>]; see there.</p>

<p class="blessed">Blessed is Hashem forever, Amain and Amain.</p>

</div>

